.TH XD\-INTL 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-intl \- Regional and Language Options
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-intl
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-intl
is Windows XP's Regional and Language Options (Control Panel):
.TP
.B Regional Options
The user's standards and formats (numbers, currency, time, date), with
samples.
Customize... changes them; the customized formats are compiled with
.BR localedef (1)
into a locale of the user's own.
.TP
.B Languages
Details... opens the input languages of
.BR xd\-keyboard (1)
(only if it is installed), beside its Text Services: the input method
and the Compose key.
.TP
.B Advanced
The system locale and the keyboard of the logon screen and text consoles,
through systemd-localed
.RB ( org.freedesktop.locale1 ),
which asks polkit, so
.BR xd\-polkit (1)
asks for a password when one is needed.
.PP
Only installed locales are offered.
Programs use new formats after the user logs off and on again.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/environment.d/60\-xeondesktop\-locale.conf
The user's formats
.RB ( LC_NUMERIC ,
.BR LC_TIME ,
\&...), which
.BR xeondesktop\-session (1)
and systemd's user manager read.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR localectl (1),
.BR locale (7),
.BR xeondesktop\-session (1)
